WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
Speaker 1: Last week after the forthcoming Roe v&nbsp;
Wade decision from the Supreme Court leaked, there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.760
was immediately speculation about who did the&nbsp;
leaking now. Much of the speculation was really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.880
in bad faith. It was right wingers arguing that&nbsp;
the real problem here is that there was a leak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:20.160
rather than the fact that women's rights are going&nbsp;
to be potentially set back by decades, thanks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:25.840
a number of activist judges placed on the Supreme&nbsp;
Court by failed former President Donald Trump. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:32.080
the issue isn't actually the leaker, but the right&nbsp;
wanted to make the leaker the issue, and the right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:41.120
immediately said, obviously, this is a left wing&nbsp;
leaker who wants to pressure justices to change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:48.000
their votes to keep Roe v Wade by making them&nbsp;
fear for their lives. And the latter, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.440
followed from there. And as I said last week,&nbsp;
we don't know the political orientation of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:59.920
leaker. There are two at least equally plausible&nbsp;
explanations. One is the leaker is on the left,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:06.800
the leaker is pro-choice. And the idea of the&nbsp;
leaker was, I'm going to leak this now so that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:12.560
the justice is planning to vote to overturn Roe v&nbsp;
Wade, will be pressured and they will be harassed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:17.520
and they might fear for their lives. And they'll&nbsp;
say, okay, okay, I'll keep Roe v Wade. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:24.560
these are appointments for life. Supreme Court&nbsp;
justices have great security. It's not super&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.160
likely that that is actually the case, but it is&nbsp;
a possibility. Just as likely is the opposite. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:35.360
again, we didn't know one way or the other, but&nbsp;
just as likely is the hypothesis that the leaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:41.520
is right wing. Why would a right winger leak the&nbsp;
decision? A right winger would leak the decision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:51.840
to make sure that by making the expected votes&nbsp;
public, none of the justices that are at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.640
as of the February draft, planning to vote&nbsp;
to overturn Roe v Wade, change their minds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:04.880
Imagine that. I don't know. Kavanaugh was on the&nbsp;
overturn Roe side back in February when the draft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:10.080
was written. But since is thinking, you know,&nbsp;
maybe I should maybe I should vote to keep it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:14.960
The idea would be a right winger leaks it to&nbsp;
put pressure on those justices not to change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:20.400
their votes. Either one is possible, but now we&nbsp;
are actually getting more and more information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:25.360
that the right wing leaker scenario is&nbsp;
the more probable one. Nina TOTENBERG,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:33.120
who is a longtime Supreme Court reporter, says&nbsp;
actually the main theory now is that this was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.520
right wing clerk who leaked this. Take a listen.
Speaker 5: In covering the court since the early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:43.680
days of Roe. How much has this leak rattled&nbsp;
the institution and the way it's viewed?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.960
Well, the way it's viewed is insidious. Quick&nbsp;
And I think within the court itself, it's an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:57.520
earthquake. There has never been a leak like this.&nbsp;
There have been minor little springs that have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:08.240
emerged from the court of reports of a a tentative&nbsp;
vote or misbehavior by one justice back in the 50,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:17.360
6070s. There were leaks, those kinds of leaks, but&nbsp;
never an entire draft of a majority opinion. That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:26.080
has never, ever occurred before. And it can only,&nbsp;
in all likelihood, have come from a justice that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:32.880
I think is less likely. Perhaps one of the clerks&nbsp;
and the leading leading theory is a conservative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:39.440
clerk who was afraid that one of the conservatives&nbsp;
might be persuaded by Chief Justice Roberts and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:46.640
to join in much more moderate opinion. And then&nbsp;
there's another theory that it was an outrage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:53.440
liberal cleric. But I think the only one that&nbsp;
makes sense is that it came from somebody who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:59.360
was afraid that this majority might not hold,&nbsp;
that Chief Justice Roberts might persuade one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:03.840
of the conservatives to come over to him.
Speaker 1: So this type of reporting is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.400
increasingly pointing to a right winger.&nbsp;
Now, we may never know, but remember,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:13.120
Ted Cruz and others were saying jail the&nbsp;
leaker. They were assuming it was a liberal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:16.640
and they were saying, you got to jail them.&nbsp;
Ted Cruz actually went on Fox News and said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:21.560
the leakers should be jailed. Remember, this.
Speaker 6: Reason it was leaked is some left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:28.400
wing presumably law clerk wanted to put political&nbsp;
pressure on the five justices that presumably are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:33.200
in the majority right now. They wanted to put&nbsp;
heat and they wanted to invoke politics to try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:39.600
to get them to change their vote. And by the&nbsp;
way, if that left wing law clerk succeeds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:45.520
it will be the most grotesque politicization of&nbsp;
the Supreme Court in the history of our nation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:50.480
You mentioned an FBI investigation. I hope&nbsp;
there is a serious one. And I hope whoever is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:57.360
responsible for this not only is fired instantly,&nbsp;
but is prosecuted and serves real jail time for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:02.240
violating the confidences of the Supreme Court.
Speaker 1: And then the last real liberal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:07.280
by which I mean a right wing reactionary,&nbsp;
Tulsi Gabbard. She went on TV and also said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:12.640
we we've got to prosecute in jail. But what's&nbsp;
the crime, Tulsi? She didn't say to be heard.&nbsp;

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:17.600
Speaker 5: I think it's also critical&nbsp;
to point out that this leak sets a very,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:22.560
very dangerous precedent for our Supreme Court&nbsp;
for three important reasons. Number one is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:27.840
first of all, this person is a thief who&nbsp;
stole this information, released it with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:33.200
very specific intent to try to incite protesters&nbsp;
and intimidate and pressure our Supreme Court&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:39.280
justices to make a political decision rather than&nbsp;
a decision that is based on the Constitution.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:46.720
Number two, we have the fact that Supreme Court&nbsp;
is not in place to legislate from the bench.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:51.440
People's representatives at the state level,&nbsp;
at the federal level are charged to make laws,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:54.480
not the Supreme Court. The Supreme&nbsp;
Court needs to make decisions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:59.520
based on the Constitution. And the Department of&nbsp;
Justice, lastly, needs to go and prosecute this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:04.000
crime, which is exactly what it is, and make&nbsp;
an example out of the person who leaked this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:09.040
information. Because our Supreme Court justices&nbsp;
cannot operate under the fear that they will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:15.840
have partizan political activists in their house&nbsp;
intimidating and threatening their ability to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.480
their job per the Constitution.
Speaker 4: And there was.&nbsp;

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:23.280
Speaker 1: Do they still want them jailed if&nbsp;
it is a right winger? But more importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:27.680
will we ever actually find out who&nbsp;
did it? I don't know that we will.

